  819  *  <br>    <code>gIOMatchedNotification</code> Delivered when an IOService object has been matched with all client drivers, and they have been probed and started.
  820  *  <br>    <code>gIOFirstMatchNotification</code> Delivered when an IOService object has been matched with all client drivers, but only once per IOService instance. Some IOService objects may be reregistered when their state is changed.
  821  *  <br>    <code>gIOWillTerminateNotification</code> Delivered after an IOService object has been terminated, during its finalize stage. Delivered after any matching on the service has finished.
  822  *  <br>    <code>gIOTerminatedNotification</code> Delivered immediately when an IOService object has been terminated, making it inactive.
  823  *   @param matching A matching dictionary to restrict notifications to only matching IOService objects. The dictionary will be released when the notification is removed, consuming the passed-in reference.
  824  *   @param handler A C function callback to deliver notifications.
  825  *   @param target An instance reference for the callback's use.
  826  *   @param ref A reference constant for the callback's use.
  827  *   @param priority A constant ordering all notifications of a each type.
  828  *   @result An instance of an IONotifier object that can be used to control or destroy the notification request. */
